# camtrap poller — its own cron file, deliberately not mixed into anyone else's.
# Install as /etc/cron.d/camtrap-poll (root:root 644). Runs as the unprivileged user that owns
# the token file, every 2 minutes (spec section 10, item 3 keeps the interval open).
# Every minute. The spec left the interval open (section 10, item 3); two minutes was chosen
# before the first live run, and a two-minute wait for the photo of someone in your room reads as
# the system not working. One ssh per minute is cheap; the box already runs a 5-minute prober.
* * * * * piuser /usr/local/bin/camtrap-poll.sh
